# Implementation Plan: Prescription Timeline Panel + Chatbot-Timeline Agentic RAG (Revised)

---

## 1. LLM Decision

| Role | Model | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| **Timeline Context Agent** | Groq Llama 3.3 70B | Fast, already integrated, handles structured JSON context, no quota risk |
| **Chat Conversation** | Groq Llama 3.3 70B | Same session, same API key, consistent |
| **Vision OCR** | Gemini 2.0 Flash | Irreplaceable for image understanding — stays scoped here only |

---

## 2. Data Flow (Source → Timeline)

```
STT / OCR → Doctor clicks "🏥 Confirm & Save to Patient Timeline Record"
   ↓
POST /api/timeline/save  (sends full Header-Body-Tail JSON + source)
   ↓
Backend: Groq Llama 3.3 70B generates a narrative VISIT SUMMARY sentence
   ↓
Stored in in-memory timeline store (Phase 1, per patientId)
   ↓
Timeline Tab (Tab 5) fetches GET /api/timeline/{patient_id} and renders cards
```

---

## 3. Visit Summary Format (Revised — User Feedback Applied)

The summary is a **natural language narrative sentence** that describes the visit event, NOT a compact dash-separated medication string.

**Format:**
> `"Patient visited CHC Nemmara and was examined by Dr. Nithin Narayanan. Diagnosed with URTI on 20 Sep 2022."`

Medications are **NOT** in the summary. They are rendered in a real-world prescription table format on the card body.

